1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,875
[Lloyd] I've been so focused
on finding it,

2
00:00:05,875 --> 00:00:07,625
I'm only realizing now,

3
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,583
I have no idea
what's waiting for me

4
00:00:09,583 --> 00:00:10,791
in that temple.

5
00:00:10,791 --> 00:00:13,208
The Arc Dragon was very...

6
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:14,458
nonspecific.

7
00:00:14,458 --> 00:00:16,333
Well, the Temple
of the Dragon Cores

8
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:18,500
was run by a helpful
spirit guardian.

9
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,166
Maybe it'll be like that?

10
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:21,416
All I know is,

11
00:00:21,416 --> 00:00:22,833
there'll be some "ritual"

12
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:24,500
to help me reach
my true potential

13
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,666
as the Green Ninja.

14
00:00:25,666 --> 00:00:27,458
The Dragon also said

15
00:00:27,458 --> 00:00:29,833
the ritual was something
you would not survive.

16
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:32,750
Yeah, trying not to think
about that part.

17
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:40,916
How do we open it?

18
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:45,083
[disembodied whispering]

19
00:00:50,458 --> 00:00:51,458
[vines rustling]

20
00:00:57,958 --> 00:00:59,541
Unh!

21
00:00:59,541 --> 00:01:01,000
Lloyd, you're sealed off!

22
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,875
It's a trap!

23
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:04,833
Oh!

24
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:08,416
Uh, or... not?

25
00:01:12,916 --> 00:01:13,958
[sighing]

26
00:01:13,958 --> 00:01:16,291
Guess I'm doing this one alone.

27
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:18,250
Or-- hear me out--

28
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:20,625
you could just not do it?

29
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:24,166
This doesn't have to be
your responsibility, Lloyd.

30
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:25,708
But it does, Arin.

31
00:01:25,708 --> 00:01:27,500
I'm the Green Ninja,

32
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,375
but I've never discovered
that true potential.

33
00:01:30,375 --> 00:01:32,208
Plus, this is
the only chance we have

34
00:01:32,208 --> 00:01:34,166
to fix the messed up state
of Elemental Energy

35
00:01:34,166 --> 00:01:35,708
in our world,

36
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:38,458
so... I have to take the risk.

37
00:01:38,458 --> 00:01:41,041
I knew you were gonna say
something like that.

38
00:01:42,666 --> 00:01:44,541
Good luck, old friend.

39
00:01:44,541 --> 00:01:46,083
See you on the other side.

40
00:02:03,541 --> 00:02:05,333
Hello?

41
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,125
Anyone?

42
00:02:08,541 --> 00:02:10,458
I'm outside now?

43
00:02:11,625 --> 00:02:12,666
Hey!

44
00:02:12,666 --> 00:02:13,541
[straining]

45
00:02:13,541 --> 00:02:14,750
Ah!

46
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,708
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

47
00:02:16,708 --> 00:02:17,875
♪ So much to see ♪

48
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:20,875
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

49
00:02:20,875 --> 00:02:22,500
♪ Together we will rise ♪

50
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,125
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

51
00:02:24,125 --> 00:02:25,583
♪ Together we will rise ♪

52
00:02:25,583 --> 00:02:28,333
♪ For what's right ♪♪

53
00:02:36,291 --> 00:02:38,208
[Rontu]
Thank you for your care,

54
00:02:38,208 --> 00:02:40,250
but like Egalt before me,

55
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:41,791
my time is near.

56
00:02:41,791 --> 00:02:44,791
No, Master Rontu,
don't say that.

57
00:02:44,791 --> 00:02:47,375
Together we'll fight
for your recovery.

58
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:49,875
I've sent Jenny and Barry
for supplies.

59
00:02:49,875 --> 00:02:51,958
I'll cook you
the most restorative bowl of--

60
00:02:51,958 --> 00:02:53,791
There is no point.

61
00:02:53,791 --> 00:02:55,000
Riyu,

62
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,625
my final student,

63
00:02:56,625 --> 00:02:58,416
also lays dying,

64
00:02:58,416 --> 00:03:00,791
somewhere in a distant land.

65
00:03:00,791 --> 00:03:03,291
What? No...

66
00:03:03,291 --> 00:03:05,625
I'm sure that's not true.

67
00:03:05,625 --> 00:03:07,208
I can feel it.

68
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:08,708
He's fading,

69
00:03:08,708 --> 00:03:10,541
passing from this life,

70
00:03:10,541 --> 00:03:11,916
as I am.

71
00:03:11,916 --> 00:03:15,416
Your suffering
must be causing bad dreams.

72
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:17,250
It's no dream,

73
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:19,458
but it is my fault.

74
00:03:19,458 --> 00:03:21,916
If I had been
a better teacher,

75
00:03:21,916 --> 00:03:24,375
I should not have let him go.

76
00:03:24,375 --> 00:03:27,458
I didn't protect him,

77
00:03:27,458 --> 00:03:28,916
and now he...

78
00:03:28,916 --> 00:03:30,666
will...

79
00:03:30,666 --> 00:03:32,625
die.

80
00:03:32,625 --> 00:03:34,541
[groaning sadly]

81
00:03:36,708 --> 00:03:40,041
[wheezing breath]

82
00:03:40,041 --> 00:03:42,083
[groaning]

83
00:03:42,083 --> 00:03:43,708
Don't worry, Riyu.

84
00:03:43,708 --> 00:03:46,041
Sora and Frak
will get you what you need.

85
00:03:46,041 --> 00:03:47,625
You'll be fine.

86
00:03:52,666 --> 00:03:54,166
Where are they?

87
00:03:54,166 --> 00:03:55,375
Why aren't they back yet?

88
00:03:56,291 --> 00:03:58,291
-[Frak] Come on!
-[both panting]

89
00:03:58,291 --> 00:03:59,750
[Frak] We gotta
catch that monster

90
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:01,916
before it destroys
everything onboard!

91
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:03,416
[Sora] I'm more worried
about getting its energy

92
00:04:03,416 --> 00:04:04,791
to save Riyu.

93
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,291
[panting]

94
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:11,291
[Frak] What direction

95
00:04:11,291 --> 00:04:12,375
do you think
that scream come from?

96
00:04:12,375 --> 00:04:13,375
[Sora] Not sure.

97
00:04:13,375 --> 00:04:14,666
We'd better split up.

98
00:04:14,666 --> 00:04:15,833
We don't have much time.

99
00:04:26,416 --> 00:04:27,416
H'up!

100
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:29,500
H'ah!

101
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:31,041
-[yelping]
-Shh!

102
00:04:31,041 --> 00:04:32,625
[Sora whispering] I thought
you were the monster.

103
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:34,166
I saw it.

104
00:04:34,166 --> 00:04:35,375
I've been trying to hide.

105
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:37,041
[Sora] You're the one
who screamed?

106
00:04:37,041 --> 00:04:38,750
Which direction did it go?

107
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:42,416
[distant high squealing]

108
00:04:42,416 --> 00:04:43,375
[squeal reverberating]

109
00:04:43,375 --> 00:04:44,875
[Sora panting]

110
00:04:47,166 --> 00:04:48,500
[squealing echoing]

111
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,375
[air squealing
through rattling slats]

112
00:04:50,375 --> 00:04:51,291
[sound stops abruptly]

113
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,416
[Sora sighing in relief]

114
00:05:05,083 --> 00:05:06,375
[Frak whispering]
Someone there?

115
00:05:11,416 --> 00:05:12,250
Who are you?

116
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:13,625
What are you doing on this ship?

117
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,291
Did you free
that elemental monster?

118
00:05:18,291 --> 00:05:19,166
Ugh!

119
00:05:19,166 --> 00:05:20,750
Get back here!

120
00:05:22,583 --> 00:05:24,291
[Frak panting]

121
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:27,333
[Sora screaming nearby]

122
00:05:27,333 --> 00:05:28,416
[Frak] Sora!

123
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:33,875
-[Sora gasping]
-[monster hissing]

124
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,875
[Sora] Ah! No!

125
00:05:37,041 --> 00:05:38,625
H'ah!

126
00:05:39,625 --> 00:05:40,875
[snarling]

127
00:05:41,958 --> 00:05:42,916
Ah!

128
00:05:43,916 --> 00:05:44,916
Nope.

129
00:05:44,916 --> 00:05:45,958
I need that!

130
00:05:50,458 --> 00:05:51,458
[monster snarling]

131
00:05:51,458 --> 00:05:52,791
[Frak] Sora!

132
00:05:54,083 --> 00:05:55,416
We can't let it escape!

133
00:05:55,416 --> 00:05:57,083
It's Riyu's only hope!

134
00:06:01,416 --> 00:06:02,875
[snarling]

135
00:06:05,416 --> 00:06:06,375
No!

136
00:06:08,083 --> 00:06:09,208
[Reggie] What?

137
00:06:09,208 --> 00:06:11,583
My creature escaped?

138
00:06:11,583 --> 00:06:13,791
What kind of Ninja are you?

139
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:16,416
That monster
is my valuable property!

140
00:06:22,458 --> 00:06:23,500
[both] H'yah!

141
00:06:24,416 --> 00:06:26,541
That's right, go get it back,

142
00:06:26,541 --> 00:06:29,083
or you'll have
the Explorer's Club of Ninjago

143
00:06:29,083 --> 00:06:30,583
to answer to!

144
00:06:30,583 --> 00:06:32,166
[groaning]

145
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:33,208
Ah!

146
00:06:33,208 --> 00:06:35,500
[boy giggling deviously]

147
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,416
[mischievous laughing]

148
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:39,208
Hello?

149
00:06:39,208 --> 00:06:41,875
A-Are you...
the Spirit of this Temple?

150
00:06:45,375 --> 00:06:47,291
[♪♪♪]

151
00:06:58,250 --> 00:07:01,166
I've seen some weird
Source Dragon visions,

152
00:07:01,166 --> 00:07:03,500
but seriously, what was that?

153
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,166
[boy] Why ask me, old man?

154
00:07:06,166 --> 00:07:07,583
No way...

155
00:07:07,583 --> 00:07:09,000
Yes way.

156
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,583
I'm the seed that grew into you,

157
00:07:11,583 --> 00:07:13,083
and you're the seed

158
00:07:13,083 --> 00:07:15,875
that will grow
into your future self.

159
00:07:15,875 --> 00:07:17,708
Well, that is,

160
00:07:17,708 --> 00:07:21,375
unless your life ends here.

161
00:07:21,375 --> 00:07:24,666
[giggling deviously]

162
00:07:24,666 --> 00:07:26,250
[Cole] Ras came through
the Monastery,

163
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:28,000
fighting everyone in his path,

164
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,291
for the library?

165
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:31,916
[Geo] This isn't the Cyrus Borg
Children's Reading Room,

166
00:07:31,916 --> 00:07:34,166
it's Master Wu's study.

167
00:07:34,166 --> 00:07:37,666
It's gotta have secrets
Ras would want, right?

168
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:38,666
[Cole] I guess.

169
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:39,791
To be honest,

170
00:07:39,791 --> 00:07:42,291
I'm not sure
what Wu kept in here.

171
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,208
Mr. Frohicky
is not going to like this.

172
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:50,291
He's got bigger problems
right now.

173
00:07:50,291 --> 00:07:52,041
Rontu isn't looking so good.

174
00:07:53,166 --> 00:07:54,541
Can't believe
I got so hotheaded

175
00:07:54,541 --> 00:07:56,541
I ran right into that fight
with Nokt.

176
00:07:56,541 --> 00:07:58,458
I could've been here,

177
00:07:58,458 --> 00:08:00,500
I could have
protected everyone from Ras.

178
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,916
Or... you'd be trapped

179
00:08:01,916 --> 00:08:04,583
wherever
all the other Ninja are.

180
00:08:04,583 --> 00:08:05,625
It can't be a coincidence

181
00:08:05,625 --> 00:08:06,833
Ras used the Gates,

182
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:09,041
then they stopped working
right after that.

183
00:08:13,458 --> 00:08:14,958
These scrolls...

184
00:08:14,958 --> 00:08:18,291
They're all about finding,
and containing, energy,

185
00:08:18,291 --> 00:08:19,250
and they're numbered,

186
00:08:19,250 --> 00:08:21,041
but one is missing,

187
00:08:21,041 --> 00:08:22,500
and one guess who took it.

188
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,250
Didn't Ras capture
a Source Dragon?

189
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:28,375
Sounds like he's pretty good
at containing energy already.

190
00:08:28,375 --> 00:08:31,250
Unless it's something specific
he needs to contain.

191
00:08:31,250 --> 00:08:34,708
Something specific
to Master Wu's knowledge.

192
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,458
[Frak and Sora panting]

193
00:08:40,458 --> 00:08:41,583
[Frak] You'd think
an Elemental Monster

194
00:08:41,583 --> 00:08:43,458
would be easier to track down.

195
00:08:43,458 --> 00:08:45,333
[distant screaming]

196
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:48,125
[Sora] I'm guessing that way.

197
00:08:49,041 --> 00:08:50,875
[villagers whimpering in panic]

198
00:08:50,875 --> 00:08:52,041
[monster snarling]

199
00:08:56,041 --> 00:08:57,083
[screaming]

200
00:08:57,083 --> 00:08:58,125
[structure crumbling]

201
00:09:00,166 --> 00:09:01,583
[snarling]

202
00:09:03,250 --> 00:09:04,583
[♪♪♪]

203
00:09:04,583 --> 00:09:05,833
[Sora] Tourists,
am I right?

204
00:09:07,041 --> 00:09:08,916
[monster snarling]

205
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:12,250
Ah!

206
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:18,000
[Sora gasping]

207
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,166
[impacts thudding]

208
00:09:20,291 --> 00:09:22,125
Can't they keep it down
out there?

209
00:09:22,125 --> 00:09:24,625
We got a hurt dragon in here!

210
00:09:24,625 --> 00:09:26,416
[Sora] Frak, keep it still!

211
00:09:26,416 --> 00:09:28,125
[Frak]
How am I supposed to do that

212
00:09:28,125 --> 00:09:29,791
when it's trying to blast me
to the Spectral Lands?

213
00:09:29,791 --> 00:09:31,791
[Riyu groaning]

214
00:09:31,791 --> 00:09:33,875
This can't be good.

215
00:09:33,875 --> 00:09:35,250
[monster snarling]

216
00:09:36,541 --> 00:09:39,583
[villagers screaming]

217
00:09:39,583 --> 00:09:40,666
Ugh!

218
00:09:40,666 --> 00:09:42,291
They had one job!

219
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:44,875
[monster snarling]

220
00:09:46,625 --> 00:09:49,500
Are you two completely
incompetent without me?

221
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,583
It's like watching Lava Tides
trying to square dance!

222
00:09:52,583 --> 00:09:54,416
Now's not the time for jokes!

223
00:09:54,416 --> 00:09:55,625
Who's joking?

224
00:09:55,625 --> 00:09:57,500
Get that energy to Riyu,

225
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,291
I can hold this thing back.

226
00:09:59,291 --> 00:10:01,583
Yeah, we, uh,
didn't get the energy yet.

227
00:10:01,583 --> 00:10:02,875
What?

228
00:10:02,875 --> 00:10:04,541
Are you two trying
to break the record

229
00:10:04,541 --> 00:10:06,958
for Most Failed Mission?

230
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:10,208
[roaring]

231
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:14,833
Ugh!

232
00:10:15,666 --> 00:10:16,708
Okay,

233
00:10:16,708 --> 00:10:18,291
I'll turn up the heat,

234
00:10:18,291 --> 00:10:19,875
you get to work.

235
00:10:19,875 --> 00:10:20,708
H'ah!

236
00:10:20,708 --> 00:10:21,541
[powers fritzing]

237
00:10:21,541 --> 00:10:22,375
Ah!

238
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:25,958
Ugh!

239
00:10:27,416 --> 00:10:30,583
I keep forgetting
about our messed up powers!

240
00:10:30,583 --> 00:10:32,333
Annoying!

241
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:34,416
We've gotta do this
the old-fashioned way.

242
00:10:34,416 --> 00:10:35,750
What does that mean?

243
00:10:35,750 --> 00:10:37,333
Take black and white pictures?

244
00:10:37,333 --> 00:10:41,208
No. Classic Ninja moves,
without Elemental Powers.

245
00:10:43,875 --> 00:10:45,208
H'yah!

246
00:10:45,208 --> 00:10:46,166
Ah!

247
00:10:49,166 --> 00:10:50,166
H'yah!

248
00:10:52,291 --> 00:10:53,666
Hi'yah!

249
00:10:57,750 --> 00:11:00,666
Uh, hope this isn't sacred
or anything.

250
00:11:00,666 --> 00:11:03,125
That flag has stood
in that spot

251
00:11:03,125 --> 00:11:05,541
for five centuries.

252
00:11:05,541 --> 00:11:06,791
Wow!

253
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:09,208
Someone's living in the past.

254
00:11:10,541 --> 00:11:11,541
Hi'yah!

255
00:11:12,791 --> 00:11:14,291
H'yah!

256
00:11:14,291 --> 00:11:15,625
H'ah! Y'ah!

257
00:11:16,666 --> 00:11:19,041
Hi'yah! Yah! Yah!

258
00:11:19,041 --> 00:11:22,000
I'm... afraid of her.

259
00:11:23,666 --> 00:11:24,875
-Hup!
-H'yah!

260
00:11:26,208 --> 00:11:28,125
[all grunting with effort]

261
00:11:28,125 --> 00:11:29,083
H'yah!

262
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:36,291
Ah!

263
00:11:36,291 --> 00:11:38,208
Sora! Now!

264
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:43,458
[device powering up]

265
00:11:44,333 --> 00:11:45,958
Riyu!

266
00:11:45,958 --> 00:11:46,916
No!

267
00:11:46,916 --> 00:11:49,125
[sighing in relief]

268
00:11:50,291 --> 00:11:51,833
Nice catch, Freya!

269
00:11:51,833 --> 00:11:52,916
[monster snarling]

270
00:11:52,916 --> 00:11:54,833
H'yah! H'ah!

271
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,375
Don't worry about us!

272
00:11:58,375 --> 00:12:00,000
Save Riyu!

273
00:12:05,250 --> 00:12:07,291
[Sora] Please be enough...

274
00:12:07,291 --> 00:12:08,583
[Riyu wheezing]

275
00:12:09,541 --> 00:12:10,583
[groaning softly]

276
00:12:11,916 --> 00:12:14,541
[bellowing]

277
00:12:17,625 --> 00:12:18,666
[Wyldfyre] H'yah!

278
00:12:21,833 --> 00:12:23,500
[Frak] Huah!

279
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:24,958
[Wyldfyre] H'ah!

280
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,916
[panting]

281
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:37,333
We need to use the environment
to our strategic advantage.

282
00:12:37,333 --> 00:12:38,333
Ugh!

283
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:40,583
Even in a fight,
you talk all boring!

284
00:12:40,583 --> 00:12:41,833
What I mean is--

285
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:43,208
force that thing
into the dead end!

286
00:12:43,208 --> 00:12:44,416
It can't escape.

287
00:12:44,416 --> 00:12:46,500
Now, that's an idea.

288
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,708
[monster snarling]

289
00:12:47,708 --> 00:12:48,958
Hah!

290
00:12:51,625 --> 00:12:53,041
H'yah!

291
00:12:56,791 --> 00:12:57,958
H'ah!

292
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:00,416
[monster hissing]

293
00:13:02,083 --> 00:13:03,291
H'yah!

294
00:13:04,291 --> 00:13:05,125
H'ah!

295
00:13:07,375 --> 00:13:09,416
Hah! H'yah!

296
00:13:13,166 --> 00:13:15,333
[energy surging]

297
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:16,791
Frak?

298
00:13:16,791 --> 00:13:18,583
It's acting all freaky!

299
00:13:22,375 --> 00:13:24,708
[monster snarling]

300
00:13:27,083 --> 00:13:28,500
[roaring]

301
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:30,583
We're going to need
a bigger dead end.

302
00:13:30,583 --> 00:13:32,333
Since when can it do that?

303
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:34,750
[monster roaring]

304
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:39,416
Are you... really me?

305
00:13:39,416 --> 00:13:41,458
I mean, young me?

306
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:43,916
[laughing]

307
00:13:43,916 --> 00:13:45,750
Why are you even asking that?

308
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:47,250
You know it's true.

309
00:13:47,250 --> 00:13:48,875
Are you here to guide me?

310
00:13:48,875 --> 00:13:50,208
[laughing]

311
00:13:50,208 --> 00:13:54,250
Does a tree guide
what happens to its seeds?

312
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,166
What's that supposed to mean?

313
00:14:00,458 --> 00:14:01,416
[blowing]

314
00:14:04,125 --> 00:14:05,083
[rumbling]

315
00:14:06,625 --> 00:14:08,041
[gasping]

316
00:14:08,041 --> 00:14:10,041
[Young Lloyd]
This is the Tree of Life.

317
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:22,625
[bursting sprouts,
trees rumbling]

318
00:14:25,833 --> 00:14:27,083
I...

319
00:14:27,083 --> 00:14:29,041
I don't understand.

320
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:34,708
Then get to the root
of the mystery.

321
00:14:40,750 --> 00:14:42,666
What am I supposed to be
looking--

322
00:14:42,666 --> 00:14:43,666
for!

323
00:14:43,666 --> 00:14:45,125
[Young Lloyd laughing]

324
00:14:47,791 --> 00:14:49,166
[sniffing] Ooh!

325
00:14:49,166 --> 00:14:51,583
Is that Merlopian seaweed cake
I smell?

326
00:14:51,583 --> 00:14:55,000
Mm! I haven't had that
since our honeymoon,

327
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,166
and it's right here
in our old neighborhood?

328
00:14:57,166 --> 00:14:59,416
Guess everything's
right here now.

329
00:14:59,416 --> 00:15:01,916
We've missed so much, Barry.

330
00:15:01,916 --> 00:15:03,083
When Arin gets back,

331
00:15:03,083 --> 00:15:05,000
he has to give us
a tour of this place.

332
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,833
If he gets back.

333
00:15:06,833 --> 00:15:07,958
I'm worried.

334
00:15:07,958 --> 00:15:10,458
Being a Ninja mom is not easy.

335
00:15:10,458 --> 00:15:13,166
We should start
a Ninja Parent support group.

336
00:15:13,166 --> 00:15:14,083
Great idea,

337
00:15:14,083 --> 00:15:15,250
but first

338
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:17,500
we gotta get everything
Mr. Frohicky needs--

339
00:15:19,375 --> 00:15:20,833
[woman] What is that?

340
00:15:20,833 --> 00:15:22,041
[man, nervously]
That's normal, right?

341
00:15:22,041 --> 00:15:23,708
[energy crackling]

342
00:15:27,291 --> 00:15:28,500
[snarling]

343
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,458
Maybe this is just

344
00:15:30,458 --> 00:15:32,375
a regular part
of the Crossroads?

345
00:15:32,375 --> 00:15:33,833
[roaring]

346
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:35,583
[yelping]

347
00:15:35,583 --> 00:15:36,625
[people screaming]

348
00:15:36,625 --> 00:15:38,416
I'm thinking no.

349
00:15:38,416 --> 00:15:39,416
[panicked screaming]

350
00:15:39,416 --> 00:15:41,208
[monster hissing]

351
00:15:42,375 --> 00:15:45,250
[roaring]

352
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:54,708
Come on, get to safety!

353
00:15:57,708 --> 00:16:01,375
[monster snarling]

354
00:16:01,375 --> 00:16:02,625
[roaring]

355
00:16:02,625 --> 00:16:04,291
Ah!

356
00:16:04,291 --> 00:16:07,916
Hey, you Gormless fopdoodle!

357
00:16:07,916 --> 00:16:12,416
Prepare to face the fury
of the Lariat Launcher!

358
00:16:12,416 --> 00:16:13,416
[blasting]

359
00:16:15,333 --> 00:16:16,916
Ugh!

360
00:16:16,916 --> 00:16:18,916
[groaning]

361
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:22,000
[Frak] Thanks for
the distraction, Gweeg!

362
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,916
My dad is so wrong about you!

363
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:31,000
Come on, Riyu.

364
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,500
This can't be it.

365
00:16:35,375 --> 00:16:37,208
<i>[Egalt] Your journey</i>

366
00:16:37,208 --> 00:16:38,833
<i>is not what you think,</i>

367
00:16:38,833 --> 00:16:40,791
<i>young Riyu.</i>

368
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:49,458
[groaning]

369
00:16:58,291 --> 00:17:01,250
Oh, her heartbeat
is getting weaker.

370
00:17:11,458 --> 00:17:13,125
[Egalt] Rest easy, Morro.

371
00:17:13,125 --> 00:17:15,750
I will handle this one.

372
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:23,458
Egalt, my love!

373
00:17:24,458 --> 00:17:26,000
I finally rejoin you,

374
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:30,083
but my passing is not
in the glory of battle

375
00:17:30,083 --> 00:17:31,916
nor the joy of peace.

376
00:17:31,916 --> 00:17:33,125
It is in failure.

377
00:17:33,125 --> 00:17:36,958
Source Dragons have abandoned
the Merged Lands.

378
00:17:36,958 --> 00:17:39,125
All is falling to pieces.

379
00:17:39,125 --> 00:17:41,708
I miss you, dear one,

380
00:17:41,708 --> 00:17:44,083
but this is not your time.

381
00:17:46,375 --> 00:17:47,750
I...

382
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,416
I don't understand.

383
00:17:49,416 --> 00:17:52,666
For good or ill,
your student is important.

384
00:17:52,666 --> 00:17:55,125
Only you can show him the way.

385
00:17:55,125 --> 00:17:58,458
The fate of this cycle
depends on it.

386
00:17:58,458 --> 00:18:00,625
But Riyu is dying.

387
00:18:00,625 --> 00:18:02,208
I can feel it.

388
00:18:02,208 --> 00:18:04,208
He is not going to make it.

389
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:07,000
Never lose hope, Rontu.

390
00:18:10,458 --> 00:18:12,666
[♪♪♪]

391
00:18:17,041 --> 00:18:18,583
[gasping]

392
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:22,083
[coughing]

393
00:18:22,083 --> 00:18:24,250
Riyu...

394
00:18:24,250 --> 00:18:26,458
[♪♪♪]

395
00:18:26,458 --> 00:18:27,916
[Wyldfyre grunting with effort]

396
00:18:27,916 --> 00:18:29,291
[heavy thudding]

397
00:18:30,583 --> 00:18:32,291
[battle thudding outside]

398
00:18:33,416 --> 00:18:34,375
[energy surging]

399
00:18:34,375 --> 00:18:36,541
[gasping]

400
00:18:36,541 --> 00:18:38,416
[monster snarling]

401
00:18:38,416 --> 00:18:39,708
Uh!

402
00:18:39,708 --> 00:18:40,708
[monster growling]

403
00:18:41,916 --> 00:18:43,041
H'yah!

404
00:18:44,333 --> 00:18:45,166
Oh!

405
00:18:47,291 --> 00:18:48,833
[snarling]

406
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:51,666
No...

407
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:54,250
[energy surging]

408
00:18:59,833 --> 00:19:01,625
[Riyu roaring]

409
00:19:03,291 --> 00:19:04,333
[gasping]

410
00:19:09,166 --> 00:19:10,333
[smashing]

411
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:17,166
[roaring]

412
00:19:20,083 --> 00:19:21,333
[roaring]

413
00:19:26,125 --> 00:19:28,583
That is the coolest thing
I've ever seen.

414
00:19:28,583 --> 00:19:31,125
That... was
a pretty powerful antidote.

415
00:19:31,125 --> 00:19:32,500
I just wanted him to live.

416
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:34,708
I had no clue this could happen.

417
00:19:34,708 --> 00:19:35,750
[monster snarling]

418
00:19:40,875 --> 00:19:41,875
[snarling]

419
00:19:48,041 --> 00:19:50,000
[Riyu growling]

420
00:19:51,041 --> 00:19:53,208
[♪♪♪]

421
00:20:10,333 --> 00:20:13,083
[bellowing in victory]

422
00:20:14,416 --> 00:20:16,125
[panting]

423
00:20:16,125 --> 00:20:17,208
[Sora] Riyu!

424
00:20:17,208 --> 00:20:19,000
Look at you, boy!

425
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,791
[Riyu grumble-talking]

426
00:20:21,791 --> 00:20:24,125
-[Sora] Oof!
-[Riyu grumbling fondly]

427
00:20:24,125 --> 00:20:26,458
That was amazing!

428
00:20:26,458 --> 00:20:27,916
We owe you our lives!

429
00:20:27,916 --> 00:20:29,958
I mean,
I totally had that thing,

430
00:20:29,958 --> 00:20:32,375
but thanks for the assist.

431
00:20:32,375 --> 00:20:34,250
[villagers celebrating]

432
00:20:34,250 --> 00:20:36,083
[Gweeg] Good show, old boy!

433
00:20:36,083 --> 00:20:38,208
Good show!

434
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:54,166
<i>[Loyalist] The monster</i>
<i>was unleashed from the airship,</i>

435
00:20:54,166 --> 00:20:57,583
<i>and it behaved</i>
<i>exactly as you predicted.</i>

436
00:20:57,583 --> 00:20:58,708
[Chief Loyalist]
Of course it did,

437
00:20:58,708 --> 00:21:00,750
but did you get
the information we need?

438
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:02,000
<i>[Loyalist] Yes.</i>

439
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,958
<i>Recorded at the precise moment</i>
<i>of expansion.</i>

440
00:21:04,958 --> 00:21:06,000
<i>Sending now.</i>

441
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,583
[Chief Loyalist]
Most interesting.

442
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:14,083
Positive news.

443
00:21:14,083 --> 00:21:17,125
We now know the exact location
of the Weapon.

444
00:21:17,125 --> 00:21:18,083
However,

445
00:21:18,083 --> 00:21:19,250
it is splintered,

446
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:21,208
in two different locations.

447
00:21:21,208 --> 00:21:22,625
but I promise,

448
00:21:22,625 --> 00:21:24,791
we will find--
and reassemble--

449
00:21:24,791 --> 00:21:27,333
the Weapon of Desolation
for you.

450
00:21:27,333 --> 00:21:28,958
<i>[Empress Beatrix]</i>
<i>Then Imperium,</i>

451
00:21:28,958 --> 00:21:29,958
<i>the Ninja,</i>

452
00:21:29,958 --> 00:21:32,375
<i>and the entire Merged Lands</i>

453
00:21:32,375 --> 00:21:34,291
<i>will bow before me</i>

454
00:21:34,291 --> 00:21:38,000
<i>as I regain my rightful power!</i>

455
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,833
All hail the good Empress.

